 random variable $X∼U[6,10],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{6+10}{2}=8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean height of the trees is $8\\,\\text{m}.$"] [17592186158002 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-6b7576a7-b188-5d29-9666-0430897568db" :answer/id #uuid "6b7576a7-b188-5d29-9666-0430897568db"] ["answer-6b7576a7-b188-5d29-9666-0430897568db" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6b7576a7-b188-5d29-9666-0430897568db" :answer/value "10\\,\\text{m}"] ["answer-d59bb3da-caf8-563a-a85b-45e4f3b2a669" :answer/id #uuid "d59bb3da-caf8-563a-a85b-45e4f3b2a669"] ["answer-d59bb3da-caf8-563a-a85b-45e4f3b2a669" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d59bb3da-caf8-563a-a85b-45e4f3b2a669" :answer/value "7.5\\,\\text{m}"] ["answer-c6d821b6-c4a4-5a46-ab4d-0167d341c182" :answer/id #uuid "c6d821b6-c4a4-5a46-ab4d-0167d341c182"] ["answer-c6d821b6-c4a4-5a46-ab4d-0167d341c182" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c6d821b6-c4a4-5a46-ab4d-0167d341c182" :answer/value "8.5\\,\\text{m}"] ["answer-47139a26-d804-59e4-870b-0b5fc3a07282" :answer/id #uuid "47139a26-d804-59e4-870b-0b5fc3a07282"] ["answer-47139a26-d804-59e4-870b-0b5fc3a07282" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-47139a26-d804-59e4-870b-0b5fc3a07282" :answer/value "8\\,\\text{m}"] ["answer-b400b317-0cb2-5752-955d-096fd7622908" :answer/id #uuid "b400b317-0cb2-5752-955d-096fd7622908"] ["answer-b400b317-0cb2-5752-955d-096fd7622908" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b400b317-0cb2-5752-955d-096fd7622908" :answer/value "9\\,\\text{m}"] [17592186156933 :answer-field/correct "answer-47139a26-d804-59e4-870b-0b5fc3a07282"] [17592186156933 :answer-field/choices "answer-6b7576a7-b188-5d29-9666-0430897568db"] [17592186156933 :answer-field/choices "answer-d59bb3da-caf8-563a-a85b-45e4f3b2a669"] [17592186156933 :answer-field/choices "answer-c6d821b6-c4a4-5a46-ab4d-0167d341c182"] [17592186156933 :answer-field/choices "answer-47139a26-d804-59e4-870b-0b5fc3a07282"] [17592186156933 :answer-field/choices "answer-b400b317-0cb2-5752-955d-096fd7622908"] [17592186158008 :question/problem "The duration of a podcast episode is uniformly distributed between $25$ and $34$ minutes. What is the expected duration of an episode?"] [17592186158008 :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the duration of a randomly chosen episode. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[25,34],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[25,34],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{25+34}{2}=29.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean duration of an episode is $29.5\\,\\text{min}.$"] [17592186158008 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-0123579c-fcde-53be-aa62-af9baaca87cb" :answer/id #uuid "0123579c-fcde-53be-aa62-af9baaca87cb"] ["answer-0123579c-fcde-53be-aa62-af9baaca87cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0123579c-fcde-53be-aa62-af9baaca87cb" :answer/value "25.5\\,\\text{min}"] ["answer-b131d1b8-1bd6-5d83-9081-be839823a988" :answer/id #uuid "b131d1b8-1bd6-5d83-9081-be839823a988"] ["answer-b131d1b8-1bd6-5d83-9081-be839823a988" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b131d1b8-1bd6-5d83-9081-be839823a988" :answer/value "29.5\\,\\text{min}"] ["answer-6ec7295d-bea7-5183-ab51-4e003202222f" :answer/id #uuid "6ec7295d-bea7-5183-ab51-4e003202222f"] ["answer-6ec7295d-bea7-5183-ab51-4e003202222f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6ec7295d-bea7-5183-ab51-4e003202222f" :answer/value "30\\,\\text{min}"] ["answer-94dcbe25-a54b-5b5d-bb4f-fe5f90e862e9" :answer/id #uuid "94dcbe25-a54b-5b5d-bb4f-fe5f90e862e9"] ["answer-94dcbe25-a54b-5b5d-bb4f-fe5f90e862e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-94dcbe25-a54b-5b5d-bb4f-fe5f90e862e9" :answer/value "34\\,\\text{min}"] ["answer-0e945b16-27df-5bf7-9478-2df2eca1e337" :answer/id #uuid "0e945b16-27df-5bf7-9478-2df2eca1e337"] ["answer-0e945b16-27df-5bf7-9478-2df2eca1e337" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0e945b16-27df-5bf7-9478-2df2eca1e337" :answer/value "59\\,\\text{min}"] [17592186156969 :answer-field/correct "answer-b131d1b8-1bd6-5d83-9081-be839823a988"] [17592186156969 :answer-field/choices "answer-0123579c-fcde-53be-aa62-af9baaca87cb"] [17592186156969 :answer-field/choices "answer-b131d1b8-1bd6-5d83-9081-be839823a988"] [17592186156969 :answer-field/choices "answer-6ec7295d-bea7-5183-ab51-4e003202222f"] [17592186156969 :answer-field/choices "answer-94dcbe25-a54b-5b5d-bb4f-fe5f90e862e9"] [17592186156969 :answer-field/choices "answer-0e945b16-27df-5bf7-9478-2df2eca1e337"] ["question-ac72fdfc-0b2a-5fb9-aa6a-78fe0b949c39" :question/id #uuid "ac72fdfc-0b2a-5fb9-aa6a-78fe0b949c39"] ["question-ac72fdfc-0b2a-5fb9-aa6a-78fe0b949c39" :question/math-academy-id "q-96924"] ["question-ac72fdfc-0b2a-5fb9-aa6a-78fe0b949c39" :question/problem "The minimum time it takes a pizzeria to deliver an order is $15$ minutes, and the maximum time is $27$ minutes. If the delivery time is uniformly distributed, what is the variance in the delivery time?"] ["question-ac72fdfc-0b2a-5fb9-aa6a-78fe0b949c39" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the time it takes to deliver a randomly selected order. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[15,27],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[15,27],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(27-15)^{2}}{12}=\\frac{144}{12}=12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the delivery time is $12\\,{\\text{min}}^{2}.$"] ["question-ac72fdfc-0b2a-5fb9-aa6a-78fe0b949c39" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-5c06d34a-873f-5c1f-bb8a-cc928f9a21e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c06d34a-873f-5c1f-bb8a-cc928f9a21e1"] ["answer-709591d7-8631-5657-ba16-1f8436e9bee0" :answer/id #uuid "709591d7-8631-5657-ba16-1